From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ori Shalom <ori.100000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:10:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: let a permission check handler only take File System
 Access away

With a permission check handler set, a File System Access grant's status
came from the handler alone: true meant GRANTED and false DENIED, so a
grant still to be asked for could never be ASK. Returning true, which an
app needs so that files the user picked keep working, also granted write
access to a file the user picked only for reading, and read and write
access to handles a site stored and restored on a later visit, without
the permission request handler being called.

Make the handler a veto: false still denies, and true keeps the grant's
own status, set by the picker, a drop, an ancestor directory or a
permission request. A grant to be asked for stays ASK, so the page must
request it and the permission request handler decides, as Chrome asks
the user.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/api/session.md                           |  2 +-
 .../file_system_access_permission_context.cc  | 10 +++-
 spec/chromium.spec.ts                         | 49 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/api/session.md b/docs/api/session.md
index ec96dafe2a..f96b90de91 100644
--- a/docs/api/session.md
+++ b/docs/api/session.md
@@ -1320,7 +1320,7 @@ session.defaultSession.setPermissionRequestHandler((webContents, permission, cal
     * `clipboard-sanitized-write` - Request access to write to the clipboard.
     * `deprecated-sync-clipboard-read` _Deprecated_ - Request access to run `document.execCommand("paste")`
     * `display-capture` - Capture the screen via the [Screen Capture API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Screen_Capture_API).
-    * `fileSystem` - Access to read, write, and file management capabilities using the [File System API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/File_System_API).
+    * `fileSystem` - Access to read, write, and file management capabilities using the [File System API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/File_System_API). The handler can only take access away: returning `true` keeps the access the page already has (a file the user picked, saved or dropped, or access granted by the permission request handler), and access the page doesn't have yet still has to be requested, which calls the permission request handler.
     * `fullscreen` - Control of the app's fullscreen state via the [Fullscreen API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Fullscreen_API).
     * `geolocation` - Access the user's geolocation data via the [Geolocation API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Geolocation_API)
     * `geolocation-approximate` - Access a coarse approximation of the user's location via the [Geolocation API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Geolocation_API).
diff --git a/shell/browser/file_system_access/file_system_access_permission_context.cc b/shell/browser/file_system_access/file_system_access_permission_context.cc
index 5458785fbf..d829096b55 100644
--- a/shell/browser/file_system_access/file_system_access_permission_context.cc
+++ b/shell/browser/file_system_access/file_system_access_permission_context.cc
@@ -372,6 +372,12 @@ class FileSystemAccessPermissionContext::PermissionGrantImpl
         path_info_{path_info} {}
 
   // FileSystemAccessPermissionGrant:
+  //
+  // The session's permission check handler can only take access away: a
+  // grant is GRANTED when it was granted (by a picker, a drop, a parent
+  // directory or a permission request) and the handler allows it. A grant
+  // still to be asked for stays ASK, so the page has to request it and the
+  // session's permission request handler decides, as Chrome asks the user.
   PermissionStatus GetStatus() override {
     DCHECK_CALLED_ON_VALID_SEQUENCE(sequence_checker_);
 
@@ -388,7 +394,9 @@ class FileSystemAccessPermissionContext::PermissionGrantImpl
       bool granted = permission_manager->CheckPermissionWithDetails(
           blink::PermissionType::FILE_SYSTEM, nullptr, origin_.GetURL(),
           std::move(details));
-      return granted ? PermissionStatus::GRANTED : PermissionStatus::DENIED;
+      if (!granted) {
+        return PermissionStatus::DENIED;
+      }
     }
 
     return status_;
